{
  "area": "Own integrations",
  "why": "Integrations come from the Environment, never MausBot's own Composio, HighLevel, Whop, MCP server registry or first-run settings import: CLI tools on PATH like composio and gh, and the MCP servers the Environment registers for every agent, Executor and Computer Use among them. Codex bots read ~/.codex/config.toml themselves; a Claude bot's isolated turn gets the user scope of ~/.claude.json forwarded with its project's .mcp.json, because Claude Code 2.1.306 reads that scope only with the user setting source, which also brings the person's settings and hooks. Upstream's switch that left the machine's own MCP servers out of Claude bots (features.claudeUserMcp, Settings' \"use my Claude Code MCP servers\") is removed with it: every bot gets the tools the Environment provides (LAZURIO.md principles 3 and 5).",
